---
/**
 * Competition — Economics-lens concept at Collective scale.
 * Emergent pressure when Identities contest scarce high-Mass allocations.
 * Cross-links Frequency tension field, inner tensor (σ_ext), Gap #65.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Competition | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Collective Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Competition
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Emergent pressure when multiple Identities contest the same limited degrees of freedom, attention, or allocations.
					The economic face of overlapping claims in a Market — and, when those claims sit on high-Mass paths, of competing curvature.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Cross-reads Frequency, the inner tension tensor, and competing-curvature work.
						Analogy, not isomorphism.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Pressure from overlapping claims.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Competition</strong> is the emergent pressure that appears when more than one Identity seeks the same scarce degrees of freedom, access, attention, or outcomes inside a Market.
					It is not hostility by default. It is the geometric fact that under scarcity, alternative claims collide.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the Economics lens, Competition belongs to the Collective scale.
					Pairwise Exchange can occur without it.
					Once a Market concentrates demand on limited high-Mass paths, Competition reveals which Preferences and which specializations hold under real pressure.
				</p>
				<p>
					When those contested paths also carry high Mass and opposing Vision Gradients, Competition is the allocation reading of a geometry the Physics lens already names:
					competing curvature in shared Space, elevated external tensor load, and Frequency mismatch.
					The two readings are not identical. They meet where scarce high-Mass allocations and opposing Stem directions occupy the same field.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Geometry bridge</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">σ<sub>ext</sub>, Frequency, competing curvature</h2>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					Frequency already treats the inner field as a high-dimensional tension continuum of competing demands.
					In the Now that field is sampled as a local stress tensor: external load from surrounding Masses (σ<sub>ext</sub>), the narrative-past component, and the future / Vision-Gradient component.
				</p>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					Another Identity contesting the same scarce path arrives first as σ<sub>ext</sub>.
					If frequencies lock destructively, energy dissipates and consistency falls.
					If high-Mass Stems generate opposing Curvature in a shared Space, each experiences the other as a strong external tensor component.
					Net causal entropy can fall. Forced synthesis can flatten Mass on at least one side.
				</p>
				<p class="text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					Economics Competition does not replace that geometry.
					It names the case in which the collision is an allocation collision: claims on the same scarce degrees of freedom under Ownership, Preference, Opportunity, and Price.
					Not every competing curvature is a Market. Not every Market pressure is a Stem war.
					The useful intersection is the contested high-Mass path.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Competition is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Emergent pressure:</strong> collision of claims on the same scarce, high-Mass degrees of freedom.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Preference revealer:</strong> under pressure, declared rankings give way to committed allocations.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Driver of Specialization:</strong> sustained Competition makes distinct roles and comparative advantage legible.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Membrane test:</strong> real Competition preserves the option to refuse, exit, or tighten jurisdiction.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Allocation reading of σ<sub>ext</sub>:</strong> when the contested object is a scarce path, economic pressure and elevated external tensor load are the same event under two lenses.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Competition is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not zero-sum identity destruction.</strong>
						Erasing another Stem is outside the lens. Mass flattening under forced synthesis is a failure mode, not a goal.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not mandatory aggression.</strong>
						Pressure can be quiet, continuous, and still binding.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with Market.</strong>
						Market is the field. Competition is the pressure that can arise inside it.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with competing curvature.</strong>
						Opposing Stem directions can exist without an allocation Market. Market pressure can exist without a Stem war.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a license to dissolve Ownership.</strong>
						Contested allocation still runs under grants and Refusal-of-Control.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Surface competing claims</strong> without forcing prestige or attention auctions.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep exit and membrane tools available under pressure.</strong>
						Identities that cannot refuse or exit are not competing; they are captured.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Use Competition to clarify specialization,</strong> not to collapse member Ownership or flatten Mass.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Read destructive resonance as a warning:</strong> if σ<sub>ext</sub> rises while consistency and causal entropy fall, the field is closer to Gap-style interference than to healthy allocation pressure.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>What scarce path is actually contested?</li>
						<li>Can each Identity refuse or exit without Stem collapse?</li>
						<li>Does this pressure clarify specialization, or only extract attention and raise dissipative σ<sub>ext</sub>?</li>
						<li>Is the collision mainly allocation (Market) or mainly opposing curvature (Stem directions) — or both?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior: <a href="/framework/market" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Market</a>.
						Next: <a href="/framework/specialization-econ" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Specialization</a>.
						Physics: <a href="/framework/frequency" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Frequency</a> (resonance vs dissonance, inner tensor),
						<a href="/framework/gravitation" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gravitation</a>.
						Open work: competing high-Mass curvatures in shared Space
						(<a href="https://github.com/identity-engineering/framework/issues/65" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gap #65</a>).
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/market" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Market</a>
					<a href="/framework/specialization-econ" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Specialization</a>
					<a href="/framework/frequency" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Frequency</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
